<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>DPIA — {{ programme }}</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
         max-width: 820px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #222; }
  h1, h2 { color: #334466; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; }
  th { background: #334466; color: #fff; }
  code { background: #f1f3f8; padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem; border-radius: 3px; }
  .risk-high { color: #a30; font-weight: bold; }
  .risk-medium { color: #a60; }
  .risk-low { color: #363; }
  footer { margin-top: 2rem; color: #666; font-size: 0.9em; border-top: 1px solid #ccc;
           padding-top: 0.6rem; }
  @media print { body { max-width: none; margin: 0; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Data Protection Impact Assessment</h1>
<p>
  <strong>Programme:</strong> {{ programme }}<br>
  <strong>Organisation:</strong> {{ organisation }}<br>
  <strong>Data controller contact:</strong> {{ data_controller }}<br>
  <strong>Generated:</strong> {{ generated_at }} (Zyuka {{ version }})
</p>

<blockquote>
  This document is a <em>starter</em>. Zyuka can summarise what it sees in
  your data; it cannot answer legal questions on your behalf. Review every
  section with your organisation's data-protection officer.
</blockquote>

<h2>1. Scope</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Retention period configured: <strong>{{ retention_days }} days</strong></li>
  <li>Small-cell suppression threshold: <strong>n &lt; {{ small_cell }}</strong></li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Nature of personal data processed</h2>
<ul>
  <li>High-risk columns: <strong>{{ scan.counts.high }}</strong></li>
  <li>Medium-risk columns: <strong>{{ scan.counts.medium }}</strong></li>
  <li>Low-risk columns: <strong>{{ scan.counts.low }}</strong></li>
</ul>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Column</th><th>Risk</th><th>Signals</th><th>Suggested action</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for col in scan.columns %}
    <tr>
      <td><code>{{ col.name }}</code></td>
      <td class="risk-{{ col.risk }}">{{ col.risk }}</td>
      <td>{{ col.signals | join(", ") }}</td>
      <td>{{ col.action }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Necessity and proportionality</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Describe the lawful basis under the Zambia Data Protection Act No. 3 of 2021.</li>
  <li>Confirm consent is collected before data entry (<code>zyuka docs consent</code>).</li>
  <li>State who may access the protected datasets and why.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Risks and mitigations</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Risk</th><th>Current mitigation</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Direct identification</td><td>Identifier columns pseudonymised (HMAC-SHA256)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Linkage across rounds</td><td>Same key reused; keys stored outside the repo</td></tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Reconstruction of small groups</td>
      <td>Cells with n &lt; {{ small_cell }} suppressed in reports</td>
    </tr>
    <tr><td>Unauthorised access</td><td>AES-GCM encryption available via <code>--encrypt</code></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>5. Outstanding actions</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Register with the Data Protection Commissioner if required.</li>
  <li>Document breach-notification procedure (72 hours).</li>
  <li>Set a review date for this DPIA.</li>
</ul>

<footer>
  Zyuka enables compliance; it does not provide it. The organisation remains the
  data controller.
</footer>

</body>
</html>
